 "fieldNotes": "From the track: Saturday, start 5:50 PM at 6,582 ft above the beach; down about 2 miles and 350 ft to the lake at 6,227 ft by 6:00; about an hour stopped at the beach (6:00 to 7:07); back up by 7:37. 4.2 miles, 371 ft of climbing, 25 minutes moving.\nFrom the photos: drone shot of the beach 7:00 PM; two sunset selfies with his wife 7:08; his wife and Marley on the shore trail.\nFrom Christian's voice note (Oct 1): Whale Beach. His wife wanted to walk with the dog and he rode the bike down. They spent time on the beach collecting carnelians that are polished; there's a vein of carnelians near that beach. The rocks look like whales, which is why it's called Whale Beach. It was a sunset trip, not sunrise. It was a great day, lovely and warm, Marley swam a lot. One of their favorite beaches.\nAI video: made from the real photo taken that day at sunset, the rocks turning into whales.\n\nFrom Christian (Oct 1): not sure if the shore is state park or forest land, so play it safe: no collecting in the public story. Wife stays unnamed. Yes to a drone loop. The carnelians probably ended up in a light jar (not stated publicly, since collecting is left out).",
